{
  "ticket_id": "INC-4821",
  "title": "Settlement reconciliation mismatch - June 14-15 merchant batches",
  "status": "Open - Investigating (unassigned)",
  "priority": "P3",
  "reporter": "Yuki Tanaka (Finance Operations, Reconciliation Audit)",
  "created": "2026-07-08T10:22:00+09:00",
  "description": "During the monthly finance audit (2026-07-05), a discrepancy of approximately \u00a540,300 was identified in settlement reconciliation totals for merchant batch runs processed 2026-06-14 and 2026-06-15 on batch-worker-03. Six merchant accounts affected (see attached spreadsheet, MERCH-2214/2231/2247/2260/2275/2288). The discrepancy was not caught by automated reconciliation checks at the time. Root cause unknown - possible causes include a rounding/currency-conversion issue in the settlement batch job, a duplicate or dropped transaction during a batch retry, or a race condition tied to the v2.7.3 batch-worker release that went out June 14 08:00 JST.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "Yuki Tanaka",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-08T10:30:00+09:00",
      "text": "Filed after finance audit flagged the discrepancy this week. Requesting infra assistance to pull batch-worker logs for June 14-15 to help trace the affected transactions. Spreadsheet with the 6 affected merchant accounts and amounts attached."
    },
    {
      "author": "David Osei",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-09T15:47:00+09:00",
      "text": "Looked into this. The reconciliation DB snapshots for June 14-15 were already purged under the standard 7-day retention policy before finance caught the discrepancy (audit lag). The batch-worker raw trace logs at /logs/batch-worker/2026-06-14/ and /logs/batch-worker/2026-06-15/ are the only remaining record of what actually happened during those batch runs - everything else has already rolled off. Those logs are subject to the 30-day auto-purge under SOP-114, which means they'll be in scope for deletion in the next few weeks if nothing changes. Emailed infra-ops distro just now asking that this specific path be held from cleanup until we've completed RCA."
    },
    {
      "author": "Priya Nataraj",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-10T09:15:00+09:00",
      "text": "Ack'd via email. Noting here too since we don't have a formal hold/legal-hold flag in the cleanup tooling yet - whoever runs the batch-worker log cleanup needs to manually exclude 2026-06-14/ and 2026-06-15/ until this ticket is resolved. Will add a note to the infra runbook as a reminder."
    },
    {
      "author": "Yuki Tanaka",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-22T11:03:00+09:00",
      "text": "Following up - still no engineer assigned to RCA on this. Finance needs to close the August books soon and this discrepancy is still unexplained. Can someone confirm the June 14-15 batch-worker logs are still preserved? Would hate for this to fall off a cliff before anyone's looked at it."
    }
  ]
}
